    "answer": {
      "short": "City A: $30.43$; City B: $31.86$. City B had the greater mean daily maximum temperature.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\overline{x}_A&=\\frac{28+31+34+32+31+29+28}{7}\\\\\\overline{x}_A&=\\frac{213}{7}\\approx30.43\\\\\\overline{x}_B&=\\frac{26+32+36+38+37+29+25}{7}\\\\\\overline{x}_B&=\\frac{223}{7}\\approx31.86\\end{align*}$$\nCity B had the greater mean daily maximum temperature because $31.86>30.43$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
